.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-ENV 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-env
.Nd OpenSSL environment variables
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The OpenSSL libraries use environment variables to override the
compiled-in default paths for various data.
To avoid security risks, the environment is usually not consulted when
the executable is set-user-ID or set-group-ID.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy CTLOG_FILE
Specifies the path to a certificate transparency log list.
See
.Xr CTLOG_STORE_new 3 .
.It Sy OPENSSL
Specifies the path to the
.Sy openssl
executable.
Used by the
.Sy rehash
script (see
.Xr openssl-rehash 1 )
and by the
.Sy CA.pl
script (see
.Xr CA.pl 1
.It Sy OPENSSL_CONF Ns , Sy OPENSSL_CONF_INCLUDE
Specifies the path to a configuration file and the directory for
included files.
See
.Xr config 5 .
.It Sy OPENSSL_CONFIG
Specifies a configuration option and filename for the
.Sy req
and
.Sy ca
commands invoked by the
.Sy CA.pl
script.
See
.Xr CA.pl 1 .
.It Sy OPENSSL_ENGINES
Specifies the directory from which dynamic engines are loaded.
See
.Xr openssl-engine 1 .
.It Sy OPENSSL_MALLOC_FD Ns , Sy OPENSSL_MALLOC_FAILURES
If built with debugging, this allows memory allocation to fail.
See
.Xr OPENSSL_malloc 3 .
.It Sy OPENSSL_MODULES
Specifies the directory from which cryptographic providers are loaded.
Equivalently, the generic
.Sy -provider-path
command-line option may be used.
.It Sy OPENSSL_TRACE
By default the OpenSSL trace feature is disabled statically.
To enable it, OpenSSL must be built with tracing support, which may be
configured like this:
.Qo Li ./config enable-trace Qc
.Pp
Unless OpenSSL tracing support is generally disabled, enable trace
output of specific parts of OpenSSL libraries, by name.
This output usually makes sense only if you know OpenSSL internals well.
.Pp
The value of this environment varialble is a comma-separated list of
names, with the following available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy TRACE
Traces the OpenSSL trace API itself.
.It Sy INIT
Traces OpenSSL library initialization and cleanup.
.It Sy TLS
Traces the TLS/SSL protocol.
.It Sy TLS_CIPHER
Traces the ciphers used by the TLS/SSL protocol.
.It Sy CONF
Show details about provider and engine configuration.
.It Sy ENGINE_TABLE
The function that is used by RSA, DSA (etc) code to select registered
ENGINEs, cache defaults and functional references (etc), will generate
debugging summaries.
.It Sy ENGINE_REF_COUNT
Reference counts in the ENGINE structure will be monitored with a line
of generated for each change.
.It Sy PKCS5V2
Traces PKCS#5 v2 key generation.
.It Sy PKCS12_KEYGEN
Traces PKCS#12 key generation.
.It Sy PKCS12_DECRYPT
Traces PKCS#12 decryption.
.It Sy X509V3_POLICY
Generates the complete policy tree at various points during X.509 v3
policy evaluation.
.It Sy BN_CTX
Traces BIGNUM context operations.
.It Sy CMP
Traces CMP client and server activity.
.It Sy STORE
Traces STORE operations.
.It Sy DECODER
Traces decoder operations.
.It Sy ENCODER
Traces encoder operations.
.It Sy REF_COUNT
Traces decrementing certain ASN.1 structure references.
.It Sy HTTP
Traces the HTTP client and server, such as messages being sent and
received.
.El
.It Sy OPENSSL_WIN32_UTF8
If set, then
.Xr UI_OpenSSL 3
returns UTF-8 encoded strings, rather than ones encoded in the current
code page, and the
.Xr openssl 1
program also transcodes the command-line parameters from the current
code page to UTF-8. This environment variable is only checked on
Microsoft Windows platforms.
.It Sy RANDFILE
The state file for the random number generator.
This should not be needed in normal use.
See
.Xr RAND_load_file 3 .
.It Sy SSL_CERT_DIR Ns , Sy SSL_CERT_FILE
Specify the default directory or file containing CA certificates.
See
.Xr SSL_CTX_load_verify_locations 3 .
.It Sy TSGET
Additional arguments for the
.Xr tsget 1
command.
.It Sy OPENSSL_ia32cap Ns , Sy OPENSSL_sparcv9cap Ns , Sy OPENSSL_ppccap Ns , Sy OPENSSL_armcap Ns , Sy OPENSSL_s390xcap Ns , Sy OPENSSL_riscvcap
OpenSSL supports a number of different algorithm implementations for
various machines and, by default, it determines which to use based on
the processor capabilities and run time feature enquiry.
These environment variables can be used to exert more control over this
selection process.
See
.Xr OPENSSL_ia32cap 3 ,
.Xr OPENSSL_s390xcap 3
and
.Xr OPENSSL_riscvcap 3 .
.It Sy NO_PROXY Ns , Sy HTTPS_PROXY Ns , Sy HTTP_PROXY
Specify a proxy hostname.
See
.Xr OSSL_HTTP_parse_url 3 .
.It Sy QLOGDIR
Specifies a QUIC qlog output directory.
See
.Xr openssl-qlog 7 .
.It Sy OSSL_QFILTER
Used to set a QUIC qlog filter specification.
See
.Xr openssl-qlog 7 .
.It Sy SSLKEYLOGFILE
Used to produce the standard format output file for SSL key logging.
Optionally set this variable to a filename to log all secrets produced
by SSL connections.
Note, use of the environment variable is predicated on configuring
OpenSSL at build time with the enable-sslkeylog feature.
The file format standard can be found at
.Lk https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-keylogfile/ .
Note: the use of
.Sy SSLKEYLOGFILE
poses an explicit security risk.
By recording the exchanged keys during an SSL session, it allows any
available party with read access to the file to decrypt application
traffic sent over that session.
Use of this feature should be restricted to test and debug environments
only.
.El
